Fix xvcServer.c so the "mmap" (UIO) build mode actually builds a UIO
binary instead of silently building the ioctl variant again.

The upstream Makefile selects the build mode purely via -DUSE_IOCTL
(passed only for the "ioctl" target, omitted for the "mmap" target),
but the source unconditionally did "#define USE_IOCTL" before the
"#ifndef USE_IOCTL" check, which forced ioctl mode regardless of the
compiler flag. Removing the unconditional define lets the Makefile's
-DUSE_IOCTL flag control the mode as documented in
jtag/zynqMP/src/user/README.md.

diff --git a/jtag/zynqMP/src/user/xvcServer.c b/jtag/zynqMP/src/user/xvcServer.c
--- a/jtag/zynqMP/src/user/xvcServer.c
+++ b/jtag/zynqMP/src/user/xvcServer.c
@@ -23,8 +23,6 @@
 #include <getopt.h>
 #include <ctype.h>

-#define USE_IOCTL
-
 #ifndef USE_IOCTL
 #define MAP_SIZE    0x10000
 static const char *UIO_PATH = "/dev/uio0";
